 lean.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tony Evers (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin's open governor's race pits Democrat David Crowley against Republican Tom Tiffany, with Tony Evers not seeking another term. Polling has been remarkably consistent: every surveyed poll since spring shows Crowley ahead, though by modest margins. The latest Marquette University poll puts him up three among likely voters, down from five in August, and headlines describe a race tightening a month before election day.\n\nTiffany holds an enormous financial advantage, raising roughly ten times more than Crowley with help from billionaire donors, and that spending is expected to test Crowley's narrow lead. Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean D, while prediction markets price Crowley's chances near 80 percent. The state's even partisan balance and the open-seat dynamic keep uncertainty high, but Crowley's steady polling edge points to a narrow Democratic advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7549, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7589, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.724, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7645, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7536, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7419, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 3.2}]}